Checkpoint. Is a &str the same size as a &String?
   &String : 1 word    an address
   &str    : 2 words   an address and a length

Every pointer to an unsized type carries the length beside the address
   &[i32]   : 2 words
   &Path    : 2 words
   Box<str> : 2 words
   &i32     : 1 word    (i32 is Sized: nothing to carry)

The owned twin is Sized: a fixed-size handle to text on the heap
   String   : 3 words   address, capacity, length
   Vec<i32> : 3 words

The length lives in the pointer, so two &str can share one start
   "hello".len() = 5, "he".len() = 2, same first byte: true
